pCloudDrive (pCloud client and drive mounter)

pCloud Drive creates a virtual drive that lets you access files stored
in pCloud as if they were local files, without keeping the complete
cloud contents on local storage. It also provides synchronization,
sharing, offline access, and desktop integration.

This SlackBuild repackages the official x86_64 AppImage. Upstream no
longer publishes a current 32-bit build, so this version is x86_64 only.

The download link in pCloudDrive.info retrieves a ZIP containing the
AppImage for this specific release through the official pCloud API.
No browser or pCloud account is required.

For a manual download, run in the SlackBuild directory:

  . ./pCloudDrive.info
  wget --content-disposition "$DOWNLOAD_x86_64"

This saves pcloud-2.3.0.zip. The SlackBuild also accepts the filename
produced by wget without --content-disposition. The MD5 in the .info
file applies to the ZIP, not to the AppImage inside it.

No dependencies outside a full Slackware 15.0 installation are expected.
The AppImage is extracted at build time and installed below
/opt/pCloudDrive.
The executable is available as /usr/bin/pCloudDrive.
